keywords: ["Zarankiewicz problem", "extremal combinatorics", "bipartite graphs", "K3,3", "SAT", "DRAT", "LRAT", "Farkas certificate", "computer-assisted proof"]
abstract: >-
  A certified proof that the largest number of ones in a 13 x 19 0/1 matrix with no 3 x 3 all-ones submatrix is 120.
  The proof splits the problem into 30 column-degree profiles, 2 478 anchor cubes and 58 186 sub-cubes, each refuted by
  an exact rational Farkas certificate of a linear relaxation or by SAT with a DRAT or LRAT proof; a standalone
  verifier re-checks it from this record alone.
